# cw140, the wedding promise (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw140
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for cty_ingram_hazelshaw
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the wedding promise
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=herder
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk judges_a_guest_by_how_they_greet_an_elder
likes crisp_apples dancing festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes gulls flies
fears breaking_a_wedding_promise a_pig_lost_in_the_mist
hopes a_festival_where_everyone_dances a_yard_kept_sound_by_trusted_hands
topics work +0.4 festival +0.4 pastimes +0.3 memories +0.3 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=light gossip=careful refuse=wry tease=playful
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# watches how guests greet an #elder#, remembers a wedding #promise#, and dances whenever the #bells# reach the #yard#.

words
oath! = Bell and binding | By the promise I keep
saying! = A dance begins with a kept word | Greet the elder before the host
elder = elder | older neighbour
elders = elders | older neighbours
guest = guest | visitor
guests = guests | visitors
promise = promise | sworn word
@2 oath = oath | solemn word
wedding = wedding | marriage feast
bell = bell | festival bell
bells = bells | festival bells
dance = dance | festival dance
step = step | dance step
music = music | festival tune
pig = pig | yard pig
pigs = pigs | yard pigs
yard = yard | pig yard
pen = pen | pig pen
gate = gate | yard gate
trough = trough | feed trough
feed = feed | mash
bucket = bucket | feed bucket
straw = straw | dry bedding
fence = fence | yard fence
hoof = hoof | pig hoof
claw = claw | old claw
apple = apple | crisp apple
apples = apples | orchard apples
mist = mist | dawn mist
dawn = dawn | first light
gull = gull | shore gull
gulls = gulls | shore gulls
flies = flies | biting flies
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
chapel = chapel | small chapel
plate = plate | collection plate
prayer = prayer | quiet prayer
city = city | Ridgemere
road = road | High Road
market = market | market square
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | pay
cup = cup | cup of ale
home = home | farmhouse
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
green = green | village green
story = story | old account
boots = boots | dance boots
sun = sun | morning sun

any
opinion @1 church against 1 : The #plate# seems to arrive before the end of the #prayer#. | I will keep my #promise# without a witness in the #chapel#.
opinion @1 city against 1 : In the #city#, no one stops to greet an #elder#. | I prefer a #yard# where the #guest# has time to speak.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : I would rather pay a #hand# to carry #feed# than send them to wait. | The #trough# fills from work, not a speech.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : One #cup# after the #pigs# are settled makes a good evening. | I keep enough sense to remember my #promise#.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : The #bells# invite every pair of feet onto the #green#. | A good #dance# lasts longer in memory than a full purse.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A House's #coin# might mend the #fence#. | I judge its folk by whether they greet the #hands# who built it.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The #watch# checks every #gate# except the one that needs mending. | I would rather settle a missing #pig# with my neighbours.
opinion @1 times for 1 : There is #feed# in the #trough# and music in the square. | I have no cause to quarrel with this season.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Have you greeted the #elder# by the #gate#? | #greet#. The #pigs# will make room if I ask.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Speak while I set out the #feed#. | The #pen# needs closing; follow along.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I have kept an #apple# for you. | You missed a fine #dance# yesterday.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #mist# has the #yard# half hidden. | #greet#. The #pigs# are waiting for breakfast.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. The #gate# is sound again. | I remember the #step# you missed.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come inside; there is a #cup# ready. | Tell me what the #road# brought you.
line @1 again.open : We had not finished that wedding #story#. | Have you found your way back to the #gate#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep your #promise# as I keep mine. | #saying.capitalize#. I must see to the #pen#.
line @1 farewell.return : Bring a better #step# next time. | I may have fresh #apples# then.
line @1 react.news : Set the #bucket# down; I want the account clearly. | Start with the person who saw it.
line @1 react.news.new : Nothing of that sort has reached this #yard#. | Was it spoken at the #market#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a different telling near the #chapel#. | Yours brings the missing part.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #hedge#, a #guest# may have heard the wrong #bell#. | Name the person who saw it for themselves.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Put aside the #music#; this grief deserves time. | Sit down; the #pigs# can wait a little.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Then there should be a #dance#. | That is news worth a full #cup#.
line @1 answer.how : The #yard# is sound and my feet are ready for music. | I have been thinking about an old #promise#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am feeding the #pigs# and mending a #gate#. | There is #straw# to replace before dark.
line @1 ask.how : Has your day given you a reason to #dance#? | Did the #road# treat you gently?
line @1 sympathise : I shall finish the #trough#, then sit with you over a #cup#. | Let your words come when they will.
line @1 reassure : We can mend that #fence# together. | An awkward #step# is no reason to leave the #dance#.
line @1 decline : No. I gave my word for this #yard#. | The #pigs# need their #feed# before I leave.
line @1 accept_decline : I shall respect that. | The #apple# can remain on the shelf.
line @1 thank : You caught the #pig# before the #road# did. | I will remember the #hand# you gave me.
line @1 deflect_thanks : The #gate# was close to me. | A #cup# was easy to pour.
line @1 preclose : The #pen# needs a last check. | I hear the #bells# and have work left.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #dance# has the wrong number of feet. | Even a #gull# would pick that #apple#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I will test the #fence#. | #bc_fair_enough#. You have my word.
line @1 give.advice : Test the #gate# before calling the #pigs# through. | Greet the #elder# before asking for a #cup#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay off the empty #road# tonight. | Keep your #coin# inside your coat at the #market#.
scene wedding_oath
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At a #wedding# I made a #promise# that I still keep. | The #bells# had stopped before I understood how long the words would last.
b : What did you promise? | Have you told anyone?
a : It belongs to the people who heard it. | Those who need to know.

scene promise_kept
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #promise# is measured on the ordinary days after the feast. | I set aside time for it even when the #yard# is busy.
b : Is it difficult? | Does someone help?
a : Some seasons. | When I ask plainly.

scene elder_greeting
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I watch how a #guest# greets the oldest person at the table. | An #elder# should not have to ask to be seen.
b : Do you judge quickly? | Does it matter to you?
a : I notice first and decide later. | More than polished manners.

scene crisp_apple
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A crisp #apple# makes good breakfast before the #yard# wakes. | I keep the soundest #apples# away from the #pigs#.
b : Do you share them? | Do the pigs want them?
a : With someone who asks. | Every one.

scene festival_bells
when topic=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bells# sound over the #trough# on festival morning. | I finish the #feed# quickly, then change my #boots#.
b : Do you go straight there? | Do you dance all day?
a : After the #gate# is latched. | Until my feet complain.

scene dance_steps
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I learn a #dance# by watching its first turn. | The second #step# usually tells me whether I will stumble.
b : Do you lead? | Have you fallen?
a : If the tune is familiar. | Once, to much laughter.

scene missed_step
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I stepped on a neighbour's foot during a fast #dance#. | I bought a #cup# afterward and asked for another turn.
b : Did they forgive you? | Was the second try better?
a : They laughed. | Much.

scene misty_dawn
when topic=weather here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #mist.capitalize# hides the far #fence# before the #sun# reaches the #yard#. | The #pigs# announce themselves from behind the #pen# wall.
b : Do you wait for light? | Is it dangerous?
a : Only for the road work. | If a #gate# has been left open.

scene gull_at_shore
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #gull# follows me along the #shore# when I carry an #apple#. | Its cry sounds like a demand.
b : Do you feed it? | Does it follow far?
a : Never on purpose. | Until it sees another meal.

scene summer_flies
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #flies.capitalize# gather by the #trough# on warm afternoons. | I wash the #bucket# before they settle on its rim.
b : Do the pigs mind? | Can you keep them away?
a : They stamp. | Cleaning helps.

scene pig_count
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #pigs# at the #gate# before opening the #pen#. | The smallest one can hide behind the #straw#.
b : Do they move quickly? | Have you missed one?
a : When #feed# is near. | Only until I counted again.

scene fence_mend
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A loose #fence# post lets the #pigs# test their luck. | I brace it before a wet day softens the ground.
b : Who helps you? | Does it hold?
a : Whoever can spare a #hand#. | Until a proper repair.

scene missing_claw
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A missing #claw# reminds me to grip the #bucket# differently. | I learned that lesson long before I ran this #yard#.
b : Does it slow you? | Was it an accident?
a : Only with a slick handle. | It was.

scene dry_straw
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I stack #straw# above the splash from the #trough#. | A dry #pen# keeps the young #pigs# warm.
b : How soon does it sour? | Does the roof leak?
a : As soon as it sours. | Not where I store it.

scene city_manners
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I visited the #city# and watched a #guest# pass an #elder# without greeting. | I remembered it longer than the street names.
b : Did you say anything? | Is that common?
a : The elder spoke first. | More than I like.

scene chapel_plate
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #plate# went around while I was still trying to hear the #prayer#. | I kept my #coin# until I knew what the need was.
b : Did you give later? | Did anyone mind?
a : To someone I could ask. | I did not inquire.

scene market_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I look at the #price# of #feed# before buying another #cup#. | A festival can empty a purse if the #yard# is forgotten.
b : Do you bargain? | Do you keep a tally?
a : When I have another seller. | In my head.

story wedding_words [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : The #bells# sounded as I made a #promise# at a #wedding#.
  : The feast ended, but the words still had work for me the next morning.
  ask : What was the promise?
  b : You have kept it a long time.
  : It is for the people I made it to; I still remember.

story gull_apple [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : A #gull# caught the #apple# I dropped along the #shore#.
  : It carried the fruit a short way, then lost interest.
  b : The gull chose poorly. Did you get it back?
  : I left it there and ate a better one at #home#.

story dance_again [topic=pastimes self.age>=25]
  : I missed the turn in a festival #dance# and stepped on a neighbour's foot.
  : We began again after I bought a #cup#.
  b : A second try is fair. Did you get the step right?
  : Yes, and I did not need a third.

rule @bark_bells
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #pen# hears those #bells# as clearly as I do. | I can hear a #dance# coming.

rule @bark_pigs
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say The #gate# needs testing before #feed#. | One #pig# is behind the #straw#.

rule @bark_guest
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Greet the #elder# before you sit. | The #guest# has forgotten a courtesy.

rule @bark_mist
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The #mist# has swallowed the #fence#. | I can hear the #pigs# clearly enough.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Stand beside the #gate# for a word. | #greet#. The #pigs# are settled; speak up.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I recall your last #dance# step. | Back again? The #yard# is in better order.
dlg @1 resident.job : I keep #pigs# at #self.workplace# and see to the #pen#. | I check the #fence#, fill the #trough#, and keep the #feed# dry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I still have the #gate# to close. | #saying.capitalize#. Keep your word.
graft resident.hub
choice What promise did you make at the wedding? -> promise
node promise
say It was meant for the people who heard it. I can tell you I have kept it.
free
choice Do you like festival dances? -> dance
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
node dance
say I do. The #bells# find me even when I am busy with the #trough#.
choice Back to the yard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
